# Configuration for scripts/ and terraform/.
#
# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in. Values set in the environment take
# precedence over this file, so a one-off override needs no edit here.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Two Cloudflare tokens, split by blast radius. The read token is safe to put
# in GitHub Actions; the write token must never leave this machine.


# READ-ONLY token. Used by scripts/analytics-snapshot.sh and by `terraform plan`
# (including the drift check in CI), so it needs more than analytics.
#
# Create at: dash.cloudflare.com -> My Profile -> API Tokens -> Create Token
#            -> "Create Custom Token"
# Permissions (add all of these):
#   Zone    | Analytics                 | Read   <- GraphQL zone analytics, for snapshots
#   Zone    | Zone                      | Read
#   Zone    | Zone Settings             | Read   <- TLS, Early Hints
#   Zone    | DNS                       | Read
#   Zone    | Zone WAF                  | Read   <- the custom ruleset
#   Zone    | Bot Management            | Read   <- add if the row exists on your plan
#   Account | Account Analytics         | Read   <- RUM / Web Analytics beacon data
#   Account | Access: Apps and Policies | Read   <- Zero Trust Access preview gate
#   Account | Cloudflare Pages          | Read   <- Pages custom domain (preview.lopes.id)
#
# If a `terraform plan` still fails on a permission, the built-in "Read all
# resources" template is a safe fallback: it is read-only by construction and
# saves iterating one missing scope at a time.
# Zone Resources:    Include -> Specific zone -> lopes.id
# Account Resources: Include -> your account
#
# The token is shown exactly once at creation — copy it before closing the page.
# Also add this one to GitHub as the CF_RO_TOKEN repository secret.
CF_RO_TOKEN=

# READ-WRITE token. Used only by `terraform apply`, only from your laptop.
# Do NOT add this to GitHub — CI plans, it never applies.
#
# Same creation path. Permissions (add five):
#   Zone    | Zone Settings             | Edit
#   Zone    | DNS                       | Edit
#   Zone    | Zone WAF                  | Edit
#   Account | Access: Apps and Policies | Edit
#   Account | Cloudflare Pages          | Edit
# Zone Resources:    Include -> Specific zone -> lopes.id
# Account Resources: Include -> your account
CF_RW_TOKEN=

# Zone ID for lopes.id.
# Find at: dash.cloudflare.com -> lopes.id -> Overview -> right sidebar,
#          under "API" (32-character hex string).
CF_ZONE_ID=

# Account ID.
# Find in any dashboard URL: dash.cloudflare.com/<account-id>/...
# It is also on Overview, in the same sidebar block as the Zone ID.
CF_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Email address allowed through Cloudflare Zero Trust Access (Email OTP) for
# preview.lopes.id and *.lopes-id.pages.dev.
# Also add to GitHub as the CF_ACCESS_EMAIL repository secret.
CF_ACCESS_EMAIL=

# Web Analytics site tag. Optional — without it the script skips the
# beacon-level query and still captures everything drawn from zone logs.
# Find in the Web Analytics URL: .../web-analytics/overview?siteTag~in=<site-tag>
CF_SITE_TAG=

# HCP Terraform (app.terraform.io) holds the Terraform state. Preferred setup is
# `terraform login`, which writes ~/.terraform.d/credentials.tfrc.json and needs
# nothing here. Set this only if you would rather keep the token in .env.
# In GitHub Actions the same value is the TF_API_TOKEN repository secret.
# TF_TOKEN_app_terraform_io=
